  "instance_name": "audience_id",
  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community is individuals who engage with internet memes, particularly those who appreciate or use motivational clichés to frame difficult tasks as noble or world-saving. This audience may include young adults and professionals who use such phrases to justify personal or organizational challenges, often in contexts of work, entrepreneurship, or activism. The meme is designed to resonate with those who are familiar with the visual language of internet culture and who may be seeking emotional or moral justification for arduous projects, potentially without fully considering the ethical implications of using Holocaust imagery. The audience is likely to be those who are desensitized to historical trauma or who are unaware of the exploitative nature of the meme, making it accessible and shareable within online communities that value 'grit' or 'sacrifice' as virtues.",
